    <string name="ddugky_1">Skill development opportunities to rural youth in the age group of 15–35 years.</string>
    <string name="ddugky_2">Industry-aligned training aimed at improving employability and access to quality job opportunities.</string>
    <string name="ddugky_3">Structured placement support upon successful completion of training.</string>
    <string name="rseti_1">Short-duration training programmes for rural youth aged 18–50 years, focusing on self-employment and micro-enterprise development.</string>
    <string name="rseti_2">Facilitates linkage with banks and credit institutions to enable establishment of individual enterprises.</string>
    <string name="rseti_3">Post-training mentoring and handholding support to ensure sustainability and growth of new businesses.</string>
    <string name="pmvishwakarma_">PM Vishwakarma</string>
    <string name="nrlm_">NRLM</string>
    <string name="pmkvy_">PMKVY</string>
    <string name="pmkvy_1">The Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship (MSDE) has been implementing its flagship scheme, Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) that aims to provide skill development training through Short-Term Training (STT) and up-skilling/re-skilling through Recognition of Prior Learning (RPL).</string>
    <string name="pmkvy_2">The scheme targets youth across the country, including rural areas.</string>
    <string name="pmkvy_3">As of 31st October 2025, there are 15,000 training centres under PMKVY across India.</string>
    <string name="pmkvy_4">PMKVY offers free skill training in industry-relevant job roles, with no course fee charged to candidates.</string>
    <string name="pmkvy_5">Candidates receive certification upon successful completion of training.</string>
    <string name="pmkvy_6">Courses are job-oriented and aligned with market demand to improve employment prospects.</string>
    <string name="pmkvy_7">On-the-job training (OJT) is provided in select job roles to offer real workplace exposure.</string>
    <string name="pmkvy_8">Training includes soft skills, digital literacy, and financial literacy to enhance overall employability.</string>
    <string name="pmkvy_9">The scheme places special focus on youth, including women, SC/ST communities, minorities and persons with disabilities.</string>
    <string name="pmkvy_10">Skill development is linked with industry needs, supporting opportunities for wage employment and self-employment.</string>

